#: includes/Admin/Help.php:142
msgid "Team access lets the holder of a WooCommerce subscription share the premium access of their subscription with guests. Each guest uses their own WordPress account and is not billed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:143
msgid "The holder invites guests by email from My account > My guests. A guest accepts the invitation, logs in or creates an account, and immediately gets the same access to premium content as the holder, through WooCommerce Memberships."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:144
msgid "Guest access follows the holder's subscription: suspended while it is on hold, kept until the end of the paid period when it is cancelled, removed when it expires."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:147
msgid "Where to find what"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:149
msgid "<strong>WooCommerce > Team access</strong>: shared subscriptions, their guests, actions and log."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:150
msgid "<strong>WooCommerce > Settings > Team access</strong>: invitation validity, sending limits, quota policy, emails, addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:151
msgid "<strong>Product edit screen</strong>: maximum number of guests for each subscription product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:152
msgid "<strong>Subscription edit screen</strong>: \"Team access\" box with the seats of the subscription."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:160
msgid "Setting up a team subscription"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:162
msgid "Edit a simple or variable subscription product and fill in <strong>Maximum number of guests</strong> in the General tab. 0 or empty disables the feature. For variable subscriptions, each variation has its own field; an empty variation field uses the product value."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:163
msgid "Make sure the product grants a WooCommerce Memberships plan (plan with \"product purchase\" access that contains this product). Guests share exactly the plans granted by the subscription."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:164
msgid "Optionally, adjust the settings in WooCommerce > Settings > Team access and the two emails in WooCommerce > Settings > Emails (\"Team access invitation\" and \"Team access invitation accepted\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:170
msgid "The quota is recorded in the subscription at purchase: changing the product later does not affect existing subscriptions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:178
msgid "For the holder (My account > My guests)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:180
msgid "<strong>Invite a user</strong>: an email with a personal link is sent. A pending invitation reserves a seat until it is accepted, cancelled or expired."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:181
msgid "<strong>Resend</strong>: a new link is sent and the previous one stops working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:182
msgid "<strong>Replace</strong>: the guest (or invitation) is removed and the seat is given to a new email address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:183
msgid "<strong>Cancel / Remove</strong>: the seat is freed and the guest immediately loses the access shared by the subscription. Their other rights (own subscription, other invitations) are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:186
msgid "For the guest"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:188
msgid "Without an account: the guest chooses a password and the account is created with the invited email address. This works even if registration is disabled on My account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:189
msgid "With an account: the guest logs in with the account that uses the invited email address, then accepts. An invitation sent to another address cannot be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:190
msgid "No password is ever sent by email, and an invitation can never set the password of an existing account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:193
msgid "Statuses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:195
msgid "<strong>Invitation pending</strong>: sent, not accepted yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:196
msgid "<strong>Invitation accepted</strong>: the guest has access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:197
msgid "<strong>Access suspended</strong>: the subscription is on hold, or the guest is over a reduced quota."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:198
msgid "<strong>Access revoked</strong>: removed by the holder or an administrator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:206
msgid "Counting seats"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:208
msgid "The holder does not use a seat. Pending invitations and accepted guests each use one. Cancelling, removing or letting an invitation expire frees the seat."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:209
msgid "The quota is the value of the product multiplied by the quantity, recorded at purchase. It is recalculated only when the customer switches plans. An administrator can force the quota of a subscription on its detail page in WooCommerce > Team access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:210
msgid "Simultaneous invitations cannot exceed the quota: seats are reserved under a database lock."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:213
#: includes/Admin/SettingsPage.php:81
msgid "When the quota decreases"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:215
msgid "Seats are ranked: accepted guests from the oldest acceptance to the most recent, then pending invitations from the oldest to the most recent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:216
msgid "With the default policy, the seats beyond the quota are suspended. Nobody is deleted, and suspended guests regain access automatically when a seat becomes available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:217
msgid "With the \"keep all guests\" policy, nobody is suspended: the overage is only reported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:218
msgid "In both cases, new invitations are blocked while the quota is exceeded, and the overage is shown to the holder and in the administration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:227
msgid "Guests have access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:228
msgid "On hold (including a failed renewal)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:228
msgid "Access suspended; restored when the subscription is reactivated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:229
msgid "Pending cancellation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:229
msgid "Access kept until the end of the paid period, then removed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:230
msgid "Cancelled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:230
msgid "Access kept while the real end date is in the future, then removed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:231
msgid "Expired, trashed or deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:231
msgid "Access removed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:232
msgid "Plan switch"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:232
msgid "New quota and new plans applied."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:235
msgid "Guest access follows the status of the holder's subscription:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:245
msgid "Every change is applied immediately, and a catch-up synchronization runs every day in case an event was missed. Running the same synchronization several times never creates duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:253
msgid "How guests get access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:255
msgid "WooCommerce Memberships still handles all content restriction. The plugin only creates a \"guest membership\" on the shared plan for each guest."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:256
msgid "A guest has at most one guest membership per plan, even when invited by several subscriptions: it stays active as long as one of them grants access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:257
msgid "Memberships bought or granted independently are never modified or deleted. If the guest already has an active membership on the plan, no guest membership is created; if it stops, the invitation takes over."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:258
msgid "If a guest later buys their own subscription, WooCommerce Memberships reuses the guest membership for the purchase: it then becomes a regular membership."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:259
msgid "If WooCommerce Memberships assigns roles to members, guests get and lose the active member role like any other member."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:262
msgid "Good to know"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:264
msgid "Guest memberships are managed by the plugin: change them from WooCommerce > Team access, not from the Memberships screens, otherwise the next synchronization restores them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:265
msgid "By default, the WooCommerce Memberships emails (activated, ending soon, ended, renewal reminder) are not sent to guests, and the Cancel and Renew actions are hidden from their members area."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:273
msgid "Administration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:275
msgid "<strong>Resynchronize</strong> a subscription from its detail page, or all of them from the list (runs in the background)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:276
msgid "<strong>Log</strong>: synchronization errors and warnings, with a banner when an error occurred in the last 7 days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:277
msgid "<strong>Invite on behalf of the holder</strong>, revoke or resend from the detail page of a subscription."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:280
msgid "Frequent questions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:282
msgid "A guest has no access: check that the subscription is active, that the product grants a Memberships plan, and that the guest is within the quota; then resynchronize the subscription."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:283
msgid "The invitation link does not work: it may have been used, cancelled, replaced by a newer invitation or have expired. Resend the invitation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:284
msgid "The guest cannot accept: they must be logged in with the account that uses the invited email address, or create an account with it."
msgstr ""

